[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20de621f-e8f8-5627-bd64-6ba71b41077b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20de621f-e8f8-5627-bd64-6ba71b41077b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544161} :answer-field/id #uuid "52688c42-4059-5864-ac3d-963accbc9ab7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b96d4599-55b6-52a4-b5e9-744fec2eb4d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-319509" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-7-3\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](images/1d/1d131288e3d38767e1d82b68777e69667711e98665101093f3b7e544e9caea1e.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{3}{7})=0.404\\,892…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)=\\pi +0.404\\,892…≈3.55,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac5709fe-0354-5d44-b05a-02a21b0da97c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6065" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544456} {:answer/id #uuid "d25214fe-4395-53a2-b548-fff04525e163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6605" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544534} {:answer/id #uuid "dbff2e28-f33a-5f18-8f52-e274e4c55978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6665" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544561} {:answer/id #uuid "e8872e6f-ba5a-570a-bbd3-ab8d4b6496ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544588} {:answer/id #uuid "fba8fc04-0fa8-577c-bd40-5fbcbbc648c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6565" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac5709fe-0354-5d44-b05a-02a21b0da97c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6065" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544456} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6c361c4-eefd-5311-9a84-4a9a4e2f34ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bc8f4760-f931-5737-8a9c-5aab0b30c4bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-132558" :question/problem "The waiting time for one customer to be served at a cafeteria varies continuously, independently, and at a constant average rate of one person served every $4$  minutes. Determine the probability that the next person is served at least $2$ minutes after the previous one. Round your answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Since the waiting time for one customer to be served at the cafeteria varies continuously, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time until serving the next person as an exponential distribution.\n\nAn exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the time needed to serve the next person. The time needed to serve the next person can be modeled as an exponential random variable. Since one person is served every $4$ minutes on average, the rate is $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{4},$ and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{4}).\n$$\n\n In this case, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-x/4}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the next person will be served at least $2$ minutes after the previous one is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/4}{|}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-{e}^{-\\infty }+{e}^{-2/4} \\\\  & =0+{e}^{-1/2} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1/2} \\\\  & ≈0.6065.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003a02a8-0d57-518b-9d54-87c8ab14787c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.58" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544087} {:answer/id #uuid "25ee0bd4-ea00-578f-a776-d6fe24e71b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544173} {:answer/id #uuid "29f70e3d-7fb0-550c-8527-ffe9105791c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544183} {:answer/id #uuid "3c35a209-2e4f-5ab8-8e85-b2749b02bdc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544220} {:answer/id #uuid "97c8c749-bb23-5bf5-acab-f511bce8e986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25ee0bd4-ea00-578f-a776-d6fe24e71b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544173} :answer-field/id #uuid "f010bca9-60ae-5099-b94b-38fd64086818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbe4274d-84e6-566b-a678-1dfe16c416af" :question/math-academy-id "q-8452" :question/problem "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=-5-3\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](images/95/9596107dc58d6acb67f1014ebc17e632dd03173aa975fa84b196588db873d8e5.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\pi <\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ If $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{5})≈0.540\\,42.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z)≈\\pi +0.540\\,42≈3.68\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caa8381d-0308-5944-b790-50b787cd73b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caa8381d-0308-5944-b790-50b787cd73b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544516} :answer-field/id #uuid "63853831-cd8f-5815-844b-593361f11ad4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d44e0172-2699-5b95-8b6b-c9e2c6a8cdf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-254581" :question/problem "A customer support team resolves tickets continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate of $1$ ticket every $5$ minutes. If a ticket has been open for $20$ minutes already, what is the probability that it will remain unresolved for at least another $10$ minutes? Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\nThe required probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since the customer support team resolves tickets continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time until the next ticket is resolved using an exponential distribution.\n\nLet $X$ be the ticket resolving time, in minutes. Since the team resolves $1$ ticket every $5$ minutes on average, the rate is $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{5}$ tickets per minute, and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{5}).\n$$\n\nRecall that exponential random variables have the memoryless property. So, given two positive real numbers $s,t,$ we have that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{5},$ $s=20,$ and $t=10.$ \n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>20+10\\,|\\,X>20) & =P(X>10) \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(1/5)\\cdot (10)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.135.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f44278-1870-59da-b693-ab5e9edbb7b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1349" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544092} {:answer/id #uuid "2fbb0c6a-76c4-5add-8d12-dd2f98f7de84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1990" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544191} {:answer/id #uuid "59c37b7d-f2a8-5b03-96d5-27b94d5bddda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1909" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544285} {:answer/id #uuid "e5302346-1455-507d-8c19-5af7fa10783e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1099" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544580} {:answer/id #uuid "eee1f799-c2f5-5fbc-b0b8-69720cd98bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1299" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5302346-1455-507d-8c19-5af7fa10783e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1099" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544580} :answer-field/id #uuid "74158e50-3525-5d26-bf97-113e74a7d386" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3898571-1060-5a54-af07-b5592b492d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132552" :question/problem "On a busy waterway, barges pass by a particular point continuously, independently, and at a constant average rate of one every $10$ minutes. Determine the probability that the next barge will pass between $5$ and $7$ minutes after the previous one. Round your answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Since barges pass continuously, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time between two successive barges using an exponential distribution.\n\nAn exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the amount of time between two successive barges. Since a barge passes every $10$ minutes, the rate is $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{10}$ barges per minute.\n\nThe time interval between two successive barges can be modeled as an exponential random variable with rate $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{10},$ and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{10}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10}{e}^{-x/10}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the next barge will pass between $5$ and $7$ minutes after the previous one is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5<X<7) & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}\\frac{1}{10}{e}^{-x/10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/10}{|}_{5}^{7} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-7/10}+{e}^{-5/10} \\\\  & ≈0.1099\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99f15c2a-e5fc-5ca0-bb85-07dbfb14f2ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.487" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99f15c2a-e5fc-5ca0-bb85-07dbfb14f2ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.487" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544422} :answer-field/id #uuid "d936cedc-6149-5dd3-984d-e6f7a43f2a04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1e2b523-bf44-5c32-9b95-836b1e8d2e60" :question/math-academy-id "q-254609" :question/problem "While riding on a road, a cyclist encounters potholes continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate of $4$ potholes per hour. If the cyclist has not encountered any potholes in the past $30$ minutes, what is the probability that he will encounter a pothole in the next $10$ minutes? Round your final answer to **three decimal places.**\n\nThe required probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since the cyclist encounters potholes continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate, we can model the time until the next pothole as an exponential distribution.\n\nLet $X$ be the time, in minutes, until the cyclist encounters the next pothole. Since the cyclist encounters, on average, $4$ potholes per hour (or $1$ pothole every $15$ minutes), the rate is $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{15}$ potholes per minute, and we can write \n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{15}).\n$$\n\nRecall that exponential random variables have the memoryless property. Therefore, given two positive real numbers $s,t,$ we have that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{15},$ $s=30,$ and $t=10.$ \n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 30+10\\,|\\,X>30) & =P(X\\le 10) \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(1/15)\\cdot (10)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-2/3} \\\\  & ≈0.487.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a3fc09a-efc9-5c4c-ac65-bd75198800e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545131} {:answer/id #uuid "7db5b616-54c4-5818-91bd-8636dfe89f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(x+\\frac{7}{2})}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545143} {:answer/id #uuid "8677d2a0-5832-5a14-aa54-22f821cce209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545148} {:answer/id #uuid "a92aeace-c06b-57c2-b93a-99dd15e0cb20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{2(y+\\frac{1}{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545156} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb38e3c-a97d-5d21-b693-c4de60dd22b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y+\\frac{1}{2}}{x+\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8677d2a0-5832-5a14-aa54-22f821cce209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545148} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3406e35-cfa3-57be-b127-de08e9b94e52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4baaba62-d9ac-5b3e-89d5-fbd516aa665c" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4ca74438b4c5e5eeae2ce46d7a86964d74adfb1e12df6029a41a04c0dea7e93.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(- \\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{1}{2})$ and has a radius of $\\frac{3}{2},$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(- \\frac{7}{2}))^{2}+(y-(- \\frac{1}{2}))^{2}={\\frac{3}{2}}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+\\frac{7}{2})+2(y+\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{1}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cc9736-1ad6-592a-aebb-e6c16d0d50e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545113} {:answer/id #uuid "1c75beaa-b238-5161-9628-8a764302e2cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545117} {:answer/id #uuid "236ef634-16e5-560d-8f85-33280287b1dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(x+\\frac{7}{2})}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545120} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3d80d9-4059-5ed3-acb0-dc16dbea0388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y-\\frac{1}{2}}{x+\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545140} {:answer/id #uuid "b6245221-7e9b-5bd2-b04e-69243f16c537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{2(y-\\frac{1}{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03cc9736-1ad6-592a-aebb-e6c16d0d50e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545113} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ed4e09-8541-5487-a559-d5ce5f6c3312" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81a754d2-b653-5f5c-a94e-7ee027cc6ddf" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3ea6262a334d81630f0d8c1b35654c7d3c74745a344587be73b1852015ed3f47.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(- \\frac{7}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ and has a radius of $\\frac{3}{2},$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(- \\frac{7}{2}))^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}={\\frac{3}{2}}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+\\frac{7}{2})+2(y-\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01090ad4-63b2-5233-bffe-b043f421a2e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{2(y+\\frac{7}{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545112} {:answer/id #uuid "52757574-b275-5ca4-8281-178bdf3acebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y+\\frac{7}{2}}{x+\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545134} {:answer/id #uuid "5c687f3a-47f7-587b-9753-63ed8bc571a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(x+\\frac{7}{2})}{y+\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545137} {:answer/id #uuid "985622cd-15fa-553a-9f98-7bd854bfacb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y+\\frac{7}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545151} {:answer/id #uuid "c015011f-bd7b-5f6b-ac3a-407f6bc8c925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ide